{
  "_id": "recurring-deposit",
  "product_name": "Recurring Deposit",
  "product_type": "deposits",
  "descriptions": {
    "summary": "A fixed amount saved every month for a chosen term, collected automatically by a recurring debit instruction into a term deposit whose interest rate is locked in at opening.",
    "key_features": [
      "Fixed monthly instalment collected automatically on the day you choose",
      "Rate locked in at opening for the whole term",
      "Terms from 6 months to 10 years",
      "Premature closure at a disclosed reduced rate",
      "Deposit insurance by DICGC up to ₹5 lakh per depositor per bank"
    ],
    "long": "Mynt reference definition (India), composed of two regulated primitives: a recurring debit mandate (a standing instruction on the customer's account with the bank, or an NACH or UPI AutoPay mandate on another bank's account) that funds a recurring term deposit. A recurring deposit is a term deposit under the RBI Master Direction on Interest Rate on Deposits (2016): the rate is fixed at opening; on premature closure interest is paid at the rate for the period run less a penalty disclosed upfront; individuals' deposits up to ₹1 crore must allow premature withdrawal. Interest is commonly compounded quarterly on each instalment from the date it is credited, and is subject to tax deducted at source above the statutory threshold. Deposit insurance by DICGC up to ₹5 lakh per depositor per bank. ASSUMPTIONS (indicative; each bank sets its own): the 6.5% rate, the 50 bps senior-citizen bonus, the 1% premature-closure penalty, the ₹100 minimum instalment, the late-instalment charge of ₹1.50 per ₹100 per month of delay, one retry three days after a failed debit, and closing the deposit after six consecutive missed instalments. A Mynt reference product names no providers, partners or risk models: the bank that offers it adds its own licence, mandate-registration handoff (with its consent purpose) and governs its own models in its GRC folder.",
    "documents": {
      "deposit_insurance": "https://www.dicgc.org.in/",
      "complaints_ombudsman": "https://cms.rbi.org.in/"
    }
  },
  "owner_entity_id": null,
  "version": 1,
  "access_mode": "open",
  "plane": {
